# FOAM mobile native architecture

## Apps

| App | Stack | Identifier |
|---|---|---|
| FOAM Driver | React Native + Expo + TypeScript | `app.foam.driver` |
| FOAM OPS | React Native + Expo + TypeScript | `app.foam.ops` |

These must be **real native** apps.

## Do not use (primary UI / architecture)

- WebView as primary UI
- Capacitor as the new architecture
- iframe / hosted website inside the app
- Next.js pages as mobile screens
- DOM-based UI or browser-only UI libraries
- HTML as the application UI
- Tailwind web classes as the mobile UI architecture

Use native React Native components and Expo-supported native APIs.

## Required native capabilities (as features need them)

- native navigation, lifecycle, permissions
- native error / loading / offline-reconnect handling
- camera, location, notifications where required
- secure local storage and platform-aware behavior where required

## Resilience — remain usable when

- network is slow or temporarily gone
- an upload fails
- permissions are denied
- the app is backgrounded, killed, or reopened
- Firebase temporarily fails
- the user taps an action multiple times

## Sharing with web

Never blindly share web UI with mobile.

Shared code only: TypeScript types, domain models, validation, business logic, pure utilities, data contracts, carefully isolated Firebase/service abstractions.
